### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:9090

### ==========================================
### STEP 0: Setup — Register and Login
### ==========================================

### 0.1 Register a test user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Cache Tester",
  "email": "cache_test@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### 0.2 Login — store response as loginRequest
# @name loginRequest
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "cache_test@example.com",
  "password": "secret123"
}

### ==========================================
### STEP 1: Verify basic CRUD still works
### ==========================================

### 1.1 Create an author
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/authors
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRequest.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fyodor Dostoevsky"
}

### 1.2 Get all authors (to find the new ID)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors

### ==========================================
### STEP 2: Test cache HIT (this is the key test)
### ==========================================

### 2.1 First GET — should be cache MISS (look at server logs)
# Replace 1 with the actual ID from step 1.1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected response: 200 OK with author JSON
### Expected server log: NO "cache hit" message (because it was a miss)
### Instead: "Failed to update cache" or no log (depends on impl)

### 2.2 Second GET — should be cache HIT
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected response: 200 OK (same as before)
### Expected server log: "cache hit: author:1"

### 2.3 Third GET — should be cache HIT again
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected server log: "cache hit: author:1"

### 2.4 10 more requests (to see consistent cache hits)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### ==========================================
### STEP 3: Test cache INVALIDATION
### ==========================================

### 3.1 Update the author — should invalidate cache
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginRequest.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Fyodor M. Dostoevsky"
}

### 3.2 GET again — should be cache MISS (cache was invalidated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected response: name is now "Fyodor M. Dostoevsky"
### Expected server log: NO "cache hit" (this was a miss)
### Cache should be re-populated with new name

### 3.3 GET again — should be cache HIT with new name
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected response: name is "Fyodor M. Dostoevsky"
### Expected server log: "cache hit: author:1"

### ==========================================
### STEP 4: Test cache MISS when key doesn't exist
### ==========================================

### 4.1 Get non-existent author — should be cache MISS
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/99999

### Expected response: 404 Not Found
### Expected server log: NO "cache hit" (was a miss)

### 4.2 Get non-existent author again — should still be cache MISS
### (we don't cache 404 responses)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/99999

### Expected response: 404 Not Found
### Expected server log: NO "cache hit" (was a miss)

### ==========================================
### STEP 5: Test DELETE invalidation
### ==========================================

### ⚠️ Only run this if you want to delete the test author

### 5.1 Delete the author — should invalidate cache
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1
# Authorization: Bearer {{loginRequest.response.body.token}}

### 5.2 Try to GET deleted author — should be 404
# GET {{baseUrl}}/api/authors/1

### Expected: 404 Not Found (no stale data from cache!)